CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ f\(\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ f<>\(\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ non-empty pointer pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
In `template <int &...>' and `template <int *... P>' the parser attached
the ellipsis to the reference or pointer type, so the parameter was not a
pack and `f()' found no match.  libc++'s std::pair default constructor is
constrained by `_CheckArgs::__enable_implicit_default<>()', declared with
`template <int &...>'.
